00:04:42.402 --> 00:04:44.360
But if people didn't have
a chance to catch it,

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:46.540
what's the high level?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.140
What is Firebase?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.140
What is this thing?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.130
ABE HASKINS: So
Firebase as a platform

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.966
started as the database.

00:04:54.966 --> 00:04:56.590
We used to have this
Realtime Database.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:57.560
We still have it, too.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.012
But we used to have
just this database.

00:05:01.012 --> 00:05:03.220
And it was this really cool
way to interact with data

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.690
and build real-time
applications.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.970
But as we progressed
with that, it

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:10.620
started to become clear that
we were solving a problem there

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.661
but there was a lot of
other problems people had.

00:05:12.661 --> 00:05:14.600
They had trouble
authenticating users.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.650
They had trouble
finding a place to put

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.970
clients ad applications, HTML,
JavaScript, stuff like that.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.330
So it started becoming
this whole platform.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.420
And today, it's
expanded even more

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.670
to be this platform of
things that most people do

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.500
that we can make easier,
things that most people need.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.570
So it's just a suite of
tools and different helpers

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:36.515
to speed up development.

00:05:36.515 --> 00:05:38.390
MARK MANDEL: And
specifically, what platforms

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.810
does Firebase work on?

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.350
ABE HASKINS: So we support a
bunch of different platforms.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.340
We have iOS, Android.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.947
We have historically a huge
presence on web, lots and lots

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.030
of JavaScript development,
AngularFire, EmberFire.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:53.240
All of those are
Firebase-specific

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.130
integrations for frameworks.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:06:00.070
We also have the C++ SDK
that is in development.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:03.260
I believe it's a beta label
now, but I'm not quite sure.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.740
But that's also out there.

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.230
MARK MANDEL: Also you've
got Unity integrations too,

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:06.580
don't you?

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.788
ABE HASKINS: We do have a
Unity integration, which is

00:06:08.788 --> 00:06:10.070
a wrap around our native SDK.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:14.380
So all the awesomeness of
those come right into Unity.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:15.590
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.980
So there's a little bit of
the history of Firebase.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:23.280
What about the new
Firebase that we all

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.750
