00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.530
the integrations are AdMob and--

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:34.630
FRANCESC CAMPOY: OK.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:35.200
ABE HASKINS: Adwords.

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.110
DOUG STEVENSON: Adwords, yeah.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:36.470
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Adwords.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.570
FRANCESC CAMPOY: And
there's also Notifications

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:39.420
and you missed--

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:39.800
DAN STEVENSON:
And Cloud Messing.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:40.290
ABE HASKINS: And the big one.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:40.360
DAN STEVENSON: Yes.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.225
ABE HASKINS: You
missed Cloud Messaging.

00:07:42.225 --> 00:07:43.142
DAN STEVENSON: Yeah.

00:07:43.142 --> 00:07:44.600
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
And also something

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.835
that-- the one that you
missed I think it's Analytics.

00:07:47.835 --> 00:07:48.615
ABE HASKINS: Yeah.

00:07:48.615 --> 00:07:49.720
DAN STEVENSON: Oh, yeah.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:50.390
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
That's Analytics.

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:51.750
DOUG STEVENSON: That's
actually a really big one,

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.916
because that supports a lot
of the other components,

00:07:53.916 --> 00:07:56.940
and all tightly very
integrated with Analytics.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.481
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah, so could
you tell us a little bit more

00:07:59.481 --> 00:08:00.790
about Analytics itself?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:01.600
DOUG STEVENSON:
Yeah, well it's--

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:02.160
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
What does it do?

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:02.800
What it does?

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:03.380
Analyzes?

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.630
DOUG STEVENSON: Yeah, so
it's an all new analyst

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.250
component that is made
for mobile devices,

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.890
so it's Android and iOS.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:13.389
It will collect and report
a lot of information

00:08:13.389 --> 00:08:15.430
about how users are using
your app automatically,

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.480
so you don't have
to write anything.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.940
But you can track your
own events on top of that.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:22.050
So you have a quota
of 500 custom events

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.310
that you can log and
parameterize yourself.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.640
And once you start to
collect all that information,

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.620
you can then turn those
events and user properties

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.990
into audiences--
actually audiences

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.780
you can define
based off of events

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.030
that have happened for a user.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.200
So you can say, everyone
who's launched my app

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.220
and gotten to, say,
level 3 in a game,

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.710
you can create an
audience just for that.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.246
You can also use the
audiences for notifications.

00:08:47.246 --> 00:08:50.050
Let's see, what else can you do?

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:52.160
You can also do funnel
analysis, and you

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:57.140
can export your data to
BigQuery for querying ad hoc.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.592
MARK MANDEL: Now I
believe this is free?

00:08:59.592 --> 00:09:01.550
DOUG STEVENSON: It is
free, and it's unlimited.

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:03.883
It's kind of hard to think
about it like that, you know,

00:09:03.883 --> 00:09:05.685
